  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to 2024 displacement in Chi&#xfa;re District, Cabo Delgado</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this UNICEF project is to provide and scale up its multi-sectoral assistance in the Chi&#xfa;re district, Cabo Delgado, in response to the deteriorating security situation and the ensuing increase in displacement and needs. UNICEF&#x2019;s response will target displaced families, affected communities, IDPs, and those who have already begun returning to their areas of origin. The response delivers life-saving interventions encompassing education, Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) , child protection, health, and nutrition to 65,260 people, of whom 12,822 are women, 11,608 are men, and 40,830 are girls. Additionally, 1,538 people with disabilities benefit from this project.</narrative>
  </description>
